<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mule xmlns="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core"
	xmlns:http="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http"
	xmlns:os="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/os"
	xmlns:ee="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core"
	xmlns:doc="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/documentation"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core/current/mule.xsd
		http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/http/current/mule-http.xsd
		http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/os http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/os/current/mule-os.xsd
		http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core/current/mule-ee.xsd">

	<!--
		GUARANTEED DELIVERY (Hohpe and Woolf): the messaging system persists a message before it acknowledges it,
		so a crash between receipt and delivery does not lose it; it is forwarded again after the restart. Here:
		a new order is written to an object store declared persistent="true" (the outbox) and only then answered
		202; a forwarder started by a Scheduler sends each stored order to the (simulated) fulfilment system and
		removes it from the outbox only after fulfilment answered 2xx. While fulfilment is down the order stays in
		the outbox and is sent again on the next run (store and forward). The order is stored in a store declared
		persistent="true"; surviving a restart is the connector's guarantee for such a store
		(https://docs.mulesoft.com/object-store-connector/latest/object-store-connector-reference), not shown by
		MUnit, which cannot restart the app: the tests show the order in that store before and after failed
		attempts.
		Each order is forwarded inside its own error handling, so one failing order never stops the pass. An order
		fulfilment rejects with a 4xx, or one still failing after eip.guaranteedDelivery.maxAttempts attempts, is
		moved aside to a quarantine store (the "dead" store, status DEAD, with the reason): retrying it would fail
		the same way, and leaving it in the outbox would retry it forever.
		POST /eip/orders/guaranteed            persists the order, then acknowledges it (202 STORED); 409 when
		                                       the orderId is already stored, delivered or dead
		GET  /eip/orders/guaranteed/{orderId}  STORED (with attempts and the last error), DELIVERED or DEAD
		(the forwarder is the flow order-forward-stored-orders, started by a Scheduler, not by a request)
		Simulated fulfilment (guaranteed-delivery-fulfilment.xml):
		POST /eip/fulfilment/orders, PUT /eip/fulfilment/availability, GET /eip/fulfilment/orders/{orderId}

		Why an object store and persistent="true": "Mule runtime engine (Mule) uses object stores to persist data
		for eventual retrieval" (https://docs.mulesoft.com/mule-runtime/latest/mule-object-stores), and the
		connector's object store has a Persistent field, "Whether the store is persistent or transient"
		(https://docs.mulesoft.com/object-store-connector/latest/object-store-connector-reference). A transient
		(in-memory) outbox loses its content when the app stops, which is exactly what this pattern prevents. On
		CloudHub a persistent store is Object Store v2; on a customer-hosted runtime it is the worker's disk, so
		one worker's outbox is not shared with another (https://docs.mulesoft.com/object-store/osv2-faq).

		With a broker the broker does this. Anypoint MQ keeps a message until the consumer acknowledges it, and
		puts an unacknowledged message back into the queue when the acknowledgment timeout passes ("Default
		Acknowledgment Timeout specifies how long a message waits before being put back into the queue ... when
		the message is not acknowledged": https://docs.mulesoft.com/mq/mq-queues). A VM queue of type PERSISTENT
		(https://docs.mulesoft.com/vm-connector/latest/vm-reference) does it inside one Mule app. MuleSoft's
		reliability pattern hands a message from a non-transactional source (like HTTP) to such a transactional
		queue (https://docs.mulesoft.com/mule-runtime/latest/reliability-patterns). This example uses neither
		broker: the outbox shows the persist-then-forward sequence that they implement.

		Why not only Until Successful: it "runs synchronously" and retries in the same event
		(https://docs.mulesoft.com/mule-runtime/latest/until-successful-scope); the attempts in progress live in
		the event, in memory, so a restart during the retries loses the message. The outbox is kept in a store
		declared persistent, which the connector keeps across restarts.

		Delivery is at least once, not exactly once: if the app stops after fulfilment answered 2xx and before the
		order is removed from the outbox, the order is sent again after the restart. The receiver must tolerate a
		repeat (an idempotent receiver, wave 1); the simulated fulfilment counts how many times it received each
		order and processes each orderId once (an os:store with failIfPresent), so the tests show a repeat
		received twice and processed once.
	-->
	<os:object-store name="eip-gd-outbox-store" doc:name="Guaranteed Delivery Outbox Object Store" persistent="true" />
	<os:object-store name="eip-gd-delivered-store" doc:name="Guaranteed Delivery Delivered Object Store" persistent="true" />
	<os:object-store name="eip-gd-dead-store" doc:name="Guaranteed Delivery Dead (Quarantine) Object Store" persistent="true" />

	<flow name="order-store-for-guaranteed-delivery" doc:description="Guaranteed delivery: persists a new order in the persistent outbox and acknowledges it (202) only after the write; the forwarder delivers it later.">
		<http:listener doc:name="POST /eip/orders/guaranteed" config-ref="http-listener-config" path="/eip/orders/guaranteed" allowedMethods="POST">
			<http:response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 202]" />
		</http:listener>
		<choice doc:name="Validate Order">
			<when expression="#[(not (payload is Object)) or isEmpty(payload.orderId)]">
				<raise-error doc:name="Raise BAD_REQUEST Error - Missing orderId" type="APP:BAD_REQUEST" description="orderId is required" />
			</when>
		</choice>
		<set-variable doc:name="SET vOrderId" variableName="vOrderId" value="#[payload.orderId]" />
		<os:contains doc:name="Check Already Delivered" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-delivered-store" target="vDelivered" />
		<os:contains doc:name="Check Already Dead" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-dead-store" target="vDead" />
		<choice doc:name="Check Order Already Handled">
			<when expression="#[vars.vDelivered or vars.vDead]">
				<raise-error doc:name="Raise CONFLICT Error - Order already handled" type="APP:CONFLICT" description="Order already received" />
			</when>
		</choice>
		<try doc:name="Try Persist New Order">
			<os:store doc:name="Persist Order In Outbox" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store" failIfPresent="true">
				<os:value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- { orderId: vars.vOrderId, order: payload, attempts: 0, storedAt: now() as String }]]]></os:value>
			</os:store>
			<error-handler>
				<on-error-propagate doc:name="On Error Propagate (orderId already in the outbox)" type="OS:KEY_ALREADY_EXISTS" logException="false">
					<raise-error doc:name="Raise CONFLICT Error - Order already stored" type="APP:CONFLICT" description="Order already received" />
				</on-error-propagate>
			</error-handler>
		</try>
		<logger doc:name="INFO: Log order stored" level="INFO" message="#['Order ' ++ vars.vOrderId ++ ' persisted in the outbox, correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
		<set-payload doc:name="Set Stored Response" value="#[output application/json --- { orderId: vars.vOrderId, status: 'STORED' }]" />
	</flow>

	<flow name="order-forward-stored-orders" doc:description="Guaranteed delivery: a Scheduler sends every order in the outbox to fulfilment; an order leaves the outbox only after fulfilment accepted it, otherwise it is sent again on the next run.">
		<scheduler doc:name="Scheduler - Forward Stored Orders" disallowConcurrentExecution="true">
			<scheduling-strategy>
				<fixed-frequency frequency="${eip.guaranteedDelivery.forwardFrequencyMillis}" timeUnit="MILLISECONDS" />
			</scheduling-strategy>
		</scheduler>
		<os:retrieve-all doc:name="Read Outbox" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store" />
		<set-variable doc:name="SET vStoredOrders" variableName="vStoredOrders" value="#[output application/java --- (payload pluck $) orderBy $.storedAt]" />
		<foreach doc:name="For Each Stored Order" collection="#[vars.vStoredOrders]">
			<flow-ref doc:name="Refer to sf-forward-one-stored-order" name="sf-forward-one-stored-order" />
		</foreach>
		<logger doc:name="INFO: Log forward run" level="INFO" message="#['Forwarder run over ' ++ sizeOf(vars.vStoredOrders) ++ ' stored orders, correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
	</flow>

	<sub-flow name="sf-forward-one-stored-order" doc:description="Sends one stored order to fulfilment; on success removes it from the outbox and records the delivery; on a 4xx, or a failure on the last allowed attempt, moves it to the dead store; on any other failure keeps it with one more attempt and the error. No failure leaves this sub-flow, so the pass goes on with the next order.">
		<set-variable doc:name="SET vStored" variableName="vStored" value="#[payload]" />
		<set-variable doc:name="SET vAttempt" variableName="vAttempt" value="#[vars.vStored.attempts + 1]" />
		<try doc:name="Try Forward One Order">
			<try doc:name="Try Forward To Fulfilment">
				<http:request doc:name="POST Order To Fulfilment" config-ref="eip-self-http-request-config" method="POST" path="/eip/fulfilment/orders">
					<http:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- vars.vStored.order]]]></http:body>
				</http:request>
				<os:store doc:name="Record Delivery" key="#[vars.vStored.orderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-delivered-store">
					<os:value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- { orderId: vars.vStored.orderId, status: 'DELIVERED', attempts: vars.vAttempt, deliveredAt: now() as String }]]]></os:value>
				</os:store>
				<os:remove doc:name="Remove Order From Outbox" key="#[vars.vStored.orderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store" />
				<error-handler>
					<on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (fulfilment rejected the order, move it aside)" type="HTTP:BAD_REQUEST, HTTP:UNAUTHORIZED, HTTP:FORBIDDEN, HTTP:NOT_FOUND, HTTP:METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED, HTTP:NOT_ACCEPTABLE, HTTP:UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE" logException="false">
						<set-variable doc:name="SET vReason" variableName="vReason" value="#['rejected by fulfilment: ' ++ error.errorType.namespace ++ ':' ++ error.errorType.identifier]" />
						<flow-ref doc:name="Refer to sf-move-order-to-dead-store" name="sf-move-order-to-dead-store" />
					</on-error-continue>
					<on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (any other failure, keep for redelivery up to the limit)" type="ANY" logException="false">
						<set-variable doc:name="SET vLastError" variableName="vLastError" value="#[error.errorType.namespace ++ ':' ++ error.errorType.identifier]" />
						<choice doc:name="Check Attempt Limit">
							<when expression="#[vars.vAttempt &gt;= (p('eip.guaranteedDelivery.maxAttempts') as Number)]">
								<set-variable doc:name="SET vReason" variableName="vReason" value="#['not delivered after ' ++ (vars.vAttempt as String) ++ ' attempts, last error ' ++ vars.vLastError]" />
								<flow-ref doc:name="Refer to sf-move-order-to-dead-store" name="sf-move-order-to-dead-store" />
							</when>
							<otherwise>
								<os:store doc:name="Keep Order In Outbox With Attempt" key="#[vars.vStored.orderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store">
									<os:value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- vars.vStored ++ { attempts: vars.vAttempt, lastError: vars.vLastError }]]]></os:value>
								</os:store>
								<logger doc:name="WARN: Log delivery failed" level="WARN" message="#['Order ' ++ vars.vStored.orderId ++ ' not delivered, kept for redelivery: ' ++ vars.vLastError ++ ', correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
							</otherwise>
						</choice>
					</on-error-continue>
				</error-handler>
			</try>
			<error-handler>
				<on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (bookkeeping failed, the order stays as it was)" type="ANY" logException="true">
					<logger doc:name="ERROR: Log order left as it was" level="ERROR" message="#['Order ' ++ vars.vStored.orderId ++ ' left in the outbox as it was: ' ++ error.errorType.identifier ++ ', correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
				</on-error-continue>
			</error-handler>
		</try>
	</sub-flow>

	<sub-flow name="sf-move-order-to-dead-store" doc:description="Moves an order aside to the dead (quarantine) store with its attempts, last error and reason, then removes it from the outbox, so the forwarder stops sending it.">
		<os:store doc:name="Store Order In Dead Store" key="#[vars.vStored.orderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-dead-store">
			<os:value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- vars.vStored ++ { status: 'DEAD', attempts: vars.vAttempt, lastError: error.errorType.namespace ++ ':' ++ error.errorType.identifier, reason: vars.vReason, deadAt: now() as String }]]]></os:value>
		</os:store>
		<os:remove doc:name="Remove Dead Order From Outbox" key="#[vars.vStored.orderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store" />
		<logger doc:name="WARN: Log order moved aside" level="WARN" message="#['Order ' ++ vars.vStored.orderId ++ ' moved to the dead store: ' ++ vars.vReason ++ ', correlationId=' ++ correlationId]" />
	</sub-flow>

	<flow name="order-get-guaranteed-delivery-status" doc:description="GET /eip/orders/guaranteed/{orderId}: STORED while the order is in the outbox, DELIVERED once fulfilment accepted it, DEAD once it was moved aside, 404 otherwise.">
		<http:listener doc:name="GET /eip/orders/guaranteed/{orderId}" config-ref="http-listener-config" path="/eip/orders/guaranteed/{orderId}" allowedMethods="GET">
			<http:response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 200]" />
		</http:listener>
		<set-variable doc:name="SET vOrderId" variableName="vOrderId" value="#[attributes.uriParams.orderId]" />
		<os:retrieve doc:name="Read Outbox Entry" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-outbox-store" target="vStored">
			<os:default-value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- {}]]]></os:default-value>
		</os:retrieve>
		<os:retrieve doc:name="Read Delivery" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-delivered-store" target="vDelivered">
			<os:default-value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- {}]]]></os:default-value>
		</os:retrieve>
		<os:retrieve doc:name="Read Dead Entry" key="#[vars.vOrderId]" objectStore="eip-gd-dead-store" target="vDead">
			<os:default-value><![CDATA[#[output application/java --- {}]]]></os:default-value>
		</os:retrieve>
		<choice doc:name="Check Order Known">
			<when expression="#[not isEmpty(vars.vStored)]">
				<set-payload doc:name="Set Stored Status" value="#[output application/json --- { orderId: vars.vOrderId, status: 'STORED', attempts: vars.vStored.attempts, (lastError: vars.vStored.lastError) if (vars.vStored.lastError != null) }]" />
			</when>
			<when expression="#[not isEmpty(vars.vDelivered)]">
				<set-payload doc:name="Set Delivered Status" value="#[output application/json --- vars.vDelivered]" />
			</when>
			<when expression="#[not isEmpty(vars.vDead)]">
				<set-payload doc:name="Set Dead Status" value="#[output application/json --- { orderId: vars.vOrderId, status: 'DEAD', attempts: vars.vDead.attempts, lastError: vars.vDead.lastError, reason: vars.vDead.reason }]" />
			</when>
			<otherwise>
				<raise-error doc:name="Raise NOT_FOUND Error - Unknown order" type="APP:NOT_FOUND" description="Order not found" />
			</otherwise>
		</choice>
	</flow>
</mule>
